Just reading through the draw code, I see a couple of potential issues.
First, x and y coords setting. You're doing it in both the large loop where you create them:
Code:
for (var i = 0; i < cols*rows; i++) {
    ...
    this._fossilPieces[i].x = col * cellSize;
    this._fossilPieces[i].y = row * cellSize;
    this._fossilPieces[i].visible = false;
    this.addChild(this._fossilPieces[i]);
};
And in the subsequent smaller loops where, I guess, you set their precise position:
Code:
for (var i = 3; i < 9; i++) {
    this._fossilPieces[i].x = (cellSize*15)+(cellSize*i);
    this._fossilPieces[i].y = (cellSize*2);
  }
You're setting x and y twice and I don't understand why. Reading through the code, it would also seem to me that you set the Y bigger than you'd want.
The first row will be set at 0, second row at cellSize*2 while you'd want it at cellSize.
Nevertheless, there are bigger issues.
You use
Code:
+ (cellSize * i)
in the smaller for loops to set X coords. Which, given that i is equal to rows * cols, means that cellSize*i reaches absurdly high numbers very quickly and makes the sprite render off screen.
If you want it to render from the left, perhaps you wanted sth like
Code:
var min = 0;
for (var i = min; i < 3; i++) {
    this._fossilPieces[i].x = (cellSize*21)+(cellSize*(i-min));
  }
min = 3;
  for (var i = min; i < 9; i++) {
    this._fossilPieces[i].x = (cellSize*15)+(cellSize*(i-min));
    this._fossilPieces[i].y = cellSize;
  }
min = 9;
  for (var i = min; i < 21; i++) {
    this._fossilPieces[i].x = (cellSize*13)+(cellSize*(i-min));
    this._fossilPieces[i].y = (cellSize*2);
  }
?
Plus, the sprites won't render at all for the most part. You set their ._visible to false in the large for loop, but when you look at the smaller for loops, you set the ._visible tag to true only in the first of the small loops. Meaning, most of your sprites will not render at all.
If you're going to render the sprites immediately, don't set the visible to false only to then immediately set it to true - it's pointless.
